        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-001" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-01 · Telegram 25986–25988&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #25986 · 2019-04-01T03:55:34:&lt;/b&gt; Here is the GSMG Puzzle! First to crack the code and retrieve a private key may keep the hidden bitcoins. Good luck to you all!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #25987 · 2019-04-01T03:55:41:&lt;/b&gt; [binary payload: 4096 bits; SHA-256 57e1a122d839c94553bc329791861aed9af5b2f3143d1faf54ead62232889e86]&lt;br&gt;8-bit byte view:&lt;br&gt;?TNIH_DN2_EHT_SI_C_REBMUN_EHT_DNA_TLUAFED_SI_31_FI_TAHW_DNA?SEGASSEM_SIH_DNES_RASEAC_DID_WOH|&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #25988 · 2019-04-01T03:55:41:&lt;/b&gt; [binary payload: 1272 bits; SHA-256 208b29e20b90939a76f016bfcb8e774ef188f259b43cb1fd86a79482f51217f9]&lt;br&gt;8-bit byte view:&lt;br&gt;00100110110011001001110010011110001100100110110010110010000100101100011000001100010010100001001010000110001011000110110010100010110010101000001001000010hvuhyhu&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Creator posts the 2019-04-01 “Here is the GSMG Puzzle!” caption and two binary payloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Primary originals of the pre-rabbit April-Fools puzzle. Their text is byte-identical to the later creator-attributed forwards in solver messages 21403–21405." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="297" width="1860" x="20" y="254" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-002" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-01 · Telegram 26065, 26083&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #26065 · 2019-04-01T14:59:15:&lt;/b&gt; First external hint:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;http://lmgtfy.com/?q=How+did+caesar+send+his+messages%3F&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #26082:&lt;/b&gt; didnt get further than this removethecorrecthinttoproceedtothe8 thing 😛&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #26083 · 2019-04-01T16:18:12:&lt;/b&gt; &amp;#x27;esrever&amp;#x27; in the bottom. Use that hint on the 2nd binary code.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Calls the Caesar query the “First external hint”; later says decoded esrever should be applied to the second binary block.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms the exact Caesar/reversal chain reconstructed in Phase 136. This is the first puzzle, not the later rabbit puzzle." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="237" width="1860" x="20" y="563" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-003" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-19 · Telegram 28507&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28507 · 2019-04-19T20:36:30:&lt;/b&gt; Well, good luck I guess.&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Media:&lt;/i&gt; photos/photo_962@19-04-2019_20-36-30.jpg&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Posts the original rabbit-puzzle JPEG with “Well, good luck I guess.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Primary Stage-0 attachment, now archived as doc/img/gsmg_stage0_original_telegram.jpg. It is distinct in bytes and resolution from the later PNG." vertex="1">
