        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-004" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-19–2019-04-20 · Telegram 28512, 28534, 28571&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28512 · 2019-04-19T20:39:38:&lt;/b&gt; If the bitcoins are still on the address the puzzle hasn&amp;#x27;t been solved yet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #28533:&lt;/b&gt; Is it a puzzle to the private keys?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28534 · 2019-04-19T23:21:58:&lt;/b&gt; 1 private key is hidden in there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #28566:&lt;/b&gt; What a kind of answer is? is a private key, or some link, or.. What result should we get?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28571 · 2019-04-20T05:28:09:&lt;/b&gt; In the end of the puzzle a private key.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says the on-chain address shows whether it is solved, that one private key is hidden, and that the puzzle ends in a private key.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Primary output/progress framing. Does not identify the derivation." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="267" width="1860" x="20" y="986" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-005" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-19 · Telegram 28522&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #28521:&lt;/b&gt; when hint? 😆&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28522 · 2019-04-19T22:03:37:&lt;/b&gt; Follow the white rabbit. 😉&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Direct reply to “when hint?”: “Follow the white rabbit.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Earliest recovered primary instance of the Stage-0 route clue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="1265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-006" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-19 · Telegram 28526, 28527&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #28525:&lt;/b&gt; i wonder how long it took to generate addresses which contained GSMG&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28526 · 2019-04-19T22:21:42:&lt;/b&gt; few seconds ;-)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28527 · 2019-04-19T22:22:16:&lt;/b&gt; Only 4 chars. The 1&amp;#x27;s take more time somehow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says generating the GSMG vanity address took seconds: “Only 4 chars. The 1’s take more time somehow.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Supports the visible GSMG/1 vanity construction. It does not make another derived GSMG-looking address a valid solution; funding or exact-address evidence is still required." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="222" width="1860" x="20" y="1454" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-007" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-20 · Telegram 28703&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28703 · 2019-04-20T19:18:24:&lt;/b&gt; Can imagine. We had to do something against bruteforcing. Just find the right next hint, good luck 😉&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says the changing web token was an anti-bruteforce measure and instructs solvers to find the correct next hint.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Explains historical form behavior; does not imply a cryptographic transform." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="147" width="1860" x="20" y="1688" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-008" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-21 · Telegram 28794, 28812&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #28791:&lt;/b&gt; as we are looking for a link and i didn&amp;#x27;t follow the logic of the puzzle yet, i scanned gsmg entirely 😂&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28794 · 2019-04-21T15:49:57:&lt;/b&gt; Won&amp;#x27;t work 😉&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #28812 · 2019-04-21T16:18:26:&lt;/b&gt; gsmg.io/puzzle&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All the info you need is there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says scanning GSMG generally “Won’t work”; later gives gsmg.io/puzzle followed by “All the info you need is there.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms the rabbit puzzle was intended to be self-contained and argues against broad site archaeology without a selected artifact." vertex="1">
