          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="2414" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-012" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-22 · Telegram 29123&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #29123 · 2019-04-22T22:25:51:&lt;/b&gt; Success detection of unlocking phase 3 is the same as you&amp;#x27;d crack any other hash.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; “Success detection of unlocking phase 3 is the same as you’d crack any other hash.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms a hash-equality gate at that solved boundary, not a hash oracle for the current endgame." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="147" width="1860" x="20" y="2603" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-013" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-04-23 · Telegram 29132&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent community context #29131 (not a direct reply edge):&lt;/b&gt; can we get the hash of phase 3? 😋&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #29132 · 2019-04-23T01:11:50:&lt;/b&gt; Nope, no hints after reaching stage 2. Hash won&amp;#x27;t help you anyhow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says that after Stage 2, another supplied hash “won’t help you anyhow.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Prevents treating every historical phase as having a creator-provided verification hash." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="2762" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-014" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-05-18 · Telegram 31990, 32043, 32044&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #31990 · 2019-05-18T03:08:15:&lt;/b&gt; Dear all, somebody pointed out that there might be a mistake in phase III of the puzzle and that is correct unfortunately. The mistake makes it nearly impossible to solve unless you&amp;#x27;d know where to add 1 extra character between the 3 answers. My sincerest apologies for this, I&amp;#x27;ll fix this a soon as I&amp;#x27;ve found a decent spot to do so as I&amp;#x27;m on holiday atm. Again, 1000 times sorry, I&amp;#x27;m aware I might have wasted a lot of time for some :-(... In order continue this is the hint for phase3: giveit = givetit.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #32043 · 2019-05-18T19:31:34:&lt;/b&gt; So, after yesterday&amp;#x27;s &amp;#x27;hint&amp;#x27; a team of puzzlers has made an unbelievable amount of progress in just one day... The progress they made was unforseen as we expected it to take at least a !month! to pass those parts of the puzzle. Hat off for those that managed to puzzle their way through all the ciphers and riddles in this extraordinary pace. We&amp;#x27;re really impressed by that, actually, we stand in awe for you. Congrats.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To those not having reached Phase III yet, no worries besides a bit of extra pressure. The &amp;quot;last&amp;quot; part of the puzzle will ensure that there&amp;#x27;s quite some time for you guys to catch up to them... although given their obvious skill this might be solved quicker than expected aswell.. time will tell. Good luck!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #32044 · 2019-05-18T19:31:49:&lt;/b&gt; In case the private key hasn&amp;#x27;t been found in 2019 we&amp;#x27;ll release a tiny hint at the start of 2020, that will be the final hint. Can the private key be retrieved without that hint? Yes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Original Phase-III typo correction, progress praise, and promise of a final 2020 hint if needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Primary provenance for records already known through the solver group; no new endgame operation." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="342" width="1860" x="20" y="2951" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-015" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4a86e8;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-04-25–2026-04-13 · Telegram 42540, 67741, 67742&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG - Community &amp;amp; support group&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #42539:&lt;/b&gt; When does the GSMG puzzle getting solved? Did you make it yourself @SoWut&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #42540 · 2020-04-25T06:31:38:&lt;/b&gt; That&amp;#x27;s up to the solvers 😁. And yes I&amp;#x27;ve put some work in it. Didn&amp;#x27;t do it entirely myself though.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #67741 · 2026-04-13T19:21:41:&lt;/b&gt; All Good Things Come To An End.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The End of GSMG Our 9 Year Chaos Tour Is Officially Over, But the Stories Stay… Forever.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hey legends.&lt;br&gt;After almost nine years of pure madness, caffeine overdoses and more red candles than any human should endure, it is time to turn the lights off.&lt;br&gt;But before we do, grab a drink, get comfortable and let me tell you the whole stupid story straight from the idiots who lived it. It all started in 2017. JRK was visiting Sydney with the better half. Instead of playing tourist like a normal person, he locked himself in a living room for nine straight days. Zero high-end programming skills. Just Siemens PLC code, some HTML, Quake 3 scripting and a bit of Pascal. He built the entire bot from scratch as one single terrifying, never-ending script. No functions. No classes. Just pure chaos and hope.&lt;br&gt;On June 10th at around 8:30 in the morning, the first order actually hit Poloniex servers. It somehow worked, albeit that the ATH of rising markets wasn’t overwritten, thus we started by selling for a loss. The very first name for this script was MR. ROIbot. And right there on that same day, d0d was already in the mix (he already knew infrastructure expert Darky, too). Greengras hooked us up with the very first server space, and the experienced algotrading coder Bloctite joined shortly after and basically saved our lives by rewriting the ENTIRE codebase (Python plus Cython, and currently basically bug-free). 1 idiot and 3 professionals with complementary skills, a host, and one big stupid dream. What could go wrong?&lt;br&gt;The reason it all started? JRK and d0d had just used another bot run by a scammer called fuzzyhobbit and thought nope. We are doing this the right way for everybody. That disrespect for the old banking system? Still burns to this day. And that is literally where Globally Supporting My Generation came from. An old friend&amp;#x27;s group name was reused and suddenly became a mission. Give the power back to the little guy.&lt;br&gt;A little later, JRK got inspired by other crypto puzzles and spent two sloppy days throwing one together. Full of grammatical mistakes and zero polish. Sorry about the mental damage. That thing is still running, and we are keeping it alive. In 40 years, he might admit he forgot how to solve it himself. The torture continues. You are welcome.&lt;br&gt;The early days were absolutely mental. Within the first few days, we were already handling around 8 million dollars in value. The market analyser and trading engine we built back then were absolute beasts; they’ve been running nearly flawlessly ever since.&lt;br&gt;We wanted to offer a proper high-end portfolio management tool to the little guy at stupidly low prices. That was always the point. (And yes, now in 2026, AI can do the same thing in one shot if you’re a prompt genius with decent subscriptions and setups. Thanks for nothing, future.)&lt;br&gt;Here is the part nobody likes to say out loud.&lt;br&gt;We never paid ourselves a single cent of salary in all these years. We had exactly one team dinner funded by GSMG. One. That is it. (Admittedly, it was a very nice dinner.) Every single subscription went straight into upgrades for Jeff Bezos&amp;#x27;s wife&amp;#x27;s latest mega yacht, and maybe even her youth.&lt;br&gt;We had some absolutely legendary moments together.&lt;br&gt;Besides the community chat banter that still makes us cry laugh at 3 am.&lt;br&gt;Boat rides with the first bunnies.&lt;br&gt;Accidentally melting an exchange by ramping our API call limit parameter times one hundred (sorry again, lads).&lt;br&gt;Some of you lost money. We know the classic move. Coin moons set the bot to 220% aggression at the top coin dumps, blame the bot. Standard crypto rite of passage. But we also saw some of you catch beautiful flash crashes and turn minutes into multiple BTC. Those wins still make us giggle like little kids.&lt;br&gt;The ride was always about getting YOU rich. Hehe. We are not here for the money; we are here for the tech. Aren’t we all? We actually meant the first part.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #67742 · 2026-04-13T19:21:41:&lt;/b&gt; So why are we stopping?&lt;br&gt;To run a bot like this in 2026, you need a ridiculous amount of compute. Our market analyser is a proper cruncher which deals with big data, all on the fly (big data by definition, fyi). It crunches numbers every microsecond, year in year out. To stay competitive, it costs a fortune. The whole setup only really makes financial sense for the big whales and UHNWIs on the highest tier. Running these calculations for the shrimps is literally killing us financially. The other subscription levels are not enough to keep it +EV. We tried. We crunched the numbers until our eyes hurt. Time to be honest and do the inevitable.&lt;br&gt;We try to be a bit ghostly, but we are definitely not ghosting you. Here is what we are doing for you right now.&lt;br&gt;The dashboard will stay open for a few days, and we’ll make sure you can retrieve your history. Also, our terms and conditions state that we have to return all funds from the last 2 weeks. We’ll make that 6 weeks instead. So, please stop sending us funds for your subscriptions.&lt;br&gt;We are not deleting the code. We are still figuring out what to do with it (maybe open source it, maybe something else, sell it to w/e company, fund or individual. We will let you know soon, or you may contact us, of course.&lt;br&gt;Your personal data was always kept to bank security grade plus standards. It will be deleted and will never be included in a sale (might that ever happen).&lt;br&gt;So thank you.&lt;br&gt;Thank you for trusting a bunch of idiots with a dream. Thank you for the memes, the rage messages, the wins, the losses and every single story you shared. This ride was never about us getting rich. It was about getting YOU rich in a world that needed it.&lt;br&gt;The lights are going off, but the story? That one lives forever.&lt;br&gt;Stay dangerous out there, stack sats and may your future entries always be better than your exits.&lt;br&gt;With love, zero regrets,&lt;br&gt;JRK, d0d, Darky, Bloctite, and the remaining GSMG crew.&lt;br&gt;P.S. The puzzle is still unsolved. We are watching from the sidelines with an infinite amount of popcorn without giving any hints - we hope that this will remain community-maintained, as the URL might vanish. 👀&lt;br&gt;P.P.S. Don’t worry about us; we’ve been busy with many non-GSMG things in the meantime. Who knows, you might enjoy some of the services/products we worked on somewhere in your life. You may find us in digital delivery systems for the entertainment and racing industry, automobile global human transport services, educational platforms, card game, logistics, data analyses, music-related entertainment, and many more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says he contributed to but did not entirely make the puzzle; the later retrospective says JRK assembled it in “two sloppy days,” with grammatical mistakes and little polish, and confirms it remains unsolved.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Strong methodological boundary: prioritize short, clue-selected mechanics and tolerate implementation mistakes; do not assume every irregularity encodes a deep secondary layer." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1077" width="1860" x="20" y="3305" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-section-02" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" value="Historical Corrections — 4 panels" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1860" x="20" y="4410" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-016" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-05-18 · Telegram 866, 867&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #866 · 2019-05-18T01:39:21:&lt;/b&gt; Dear all, somebody pointed out that there might be a mistake in phase III and that is correct unfortunately. The mistake makes it nearly impossible to solve unless you&amp;#x27;d know where to add 1 extra character between the 3 answers. My sincerest apologies for this, I&amp;#x27;ll fix this a soon as I&amp;#x27;ve found a decent spot to do so as I&amp;#x27;m on holiday atm. Again, 1000 times sorry, I&amp;#x27;m aware I might have wasted a lot of time for some :-(...&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #867 · 2019-05-18T01:43:46:&lt;/b&gt; Here&amp;#x27;s the hint in order to bypass the mistake:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;giveit = givetit&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Creator admits a Phase III error and gives giveit = givetit.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Genuine correction for an earlier solved phase, not a Cosmic Duality clue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="237" width="1860" x="20" y="4462" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-017" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-05-18 · Telegram 879&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #879 · 2019-05-18T19:26:26:&lt;/b&gt; So, after yesterday&amp;#x27;s &amp;#x27;hint&amp;#x27; a team of puzzlers has made an unbelievable amount of progress in just one day... The progress they made was unforseen as we expected it to take at least a !month! to pass those parts of the puzzle. Hat off for those that managed to puzzle their way through all the ciphers and riddles in this extraordinary pace. We&amp;#x27;re really impressed by that, actually, we stand in awe for you. Congrats.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To those not having reached Phase III yet, no worries besides a bit of extra pressure. The &amp;quot;last&amp;quot; part of the puzzle will ensure that there&amp;#x27;s quite some time for you guys to catch up to them... although given their obvious skill this might be solved quicker than expected aswell.. time will tell. Good luck!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Praises the team’s unexpectedly rapid post-correction progress.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Progress signal only." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="222" width="1860" x="20" y="4711" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-018" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2019-05-18 · Telegram 881&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #881 · 2019-05-18T19:31:02:&lt;/b&gt; In case the private key hasn&amp;#x27;t been found in 2019 we&amp;#x27;ll release a tiny hint at the start of 2020, that will be the final hint. Can the private key be retrieved without that hint? Yes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says a final hint would arrive in 2020 if needed and the key was recoverable without it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Establishes intended solvability, not an operation." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="162" width="1860" x="20" y="4945" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-019" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-02-22 · Telegram 1806&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #1806 · 2020-02-22T18:11:52:&lt;/b&gt; Typos: Horrible mistakes due to rushed work. I&amp;#x27;m 100% to blame for this noobish display of words. No clues to be found in those typos might you wonder 😉.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Explicitly says rushed typos contain no clues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Closes typo-mining." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="162" width="1860" x="20" y="5119" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-section-03" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" value="First Piece and Extra Door — 17 panels" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1860" x="20" y="5309" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-020" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-01-14 · Telegram 1710&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #1710 · 2020-01-14T12:38:06:&lt;/b&gt; Roses are White but often Red.&lt;br&gt;Yellow has a number and so does Blue.&lt;br&gt;Go back to the first puzzle piece without further ado.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It might have shown you only one door, beware that the rabbits nest may contain a whole lot more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hush hush.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; “Yellow has a number and so does Blue”; return to the first puzzle piece; rabbits’ nest may contain more than one door.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Primary first-piece color/door clue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="237" width="1860" x="20" y="5361" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-021" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-04-08 · Telegram 3338&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #3338 · 2020-04-08T21:38:10:&lt;/b&gt; Those hints are the last hints. Although I can say that one team managed to find something... something others haven&amp;#x27;t yet found (unless they didn&amp;#x27;t tell us).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says one team found something others had not.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Progress signal; no method disclosed." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="162" width="1860" x="20" y="5610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-022" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-04-08 · Telegram 3391&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #3391 · 2020-04-08T23:33:48:&lt;/b&gt; (not a hint btw, just fooling around)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Explicitly says a nearby comment is “not a hint.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Do not mine that joke." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="147" width="1860" x="20" y="5784" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-023" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-05-21 · Telegram 4094, 4096&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #4076:&lt;/b&gt; The January hint is missing on github, isn&amp;#x27;t it?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4094 · 2020-05-21T01:54:11:&lt;/b&gt; It is&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #1710:&lt;/b&gt; Roses are White but often Red.&lt;br&gt;Yellow has a number and so does Blue.&lt;br&gt;Go back to the first puzzle piece without further ado.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It might have shown you only one door, beware that the rabbits nest may contain a whole lot more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hush hush.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4096 · 2020-05-21T02:36:55:&lt;/b&gt; This one 👆.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms the January hint was missing from GitHub and points back to message 1710.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Locks the intended official hint text." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="327" width="1860" x="20" y="5943" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-024" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-05-21 · Telegram 4102, 4105&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4102 · 2020-05-21T05:40:46:&lt;/b&gt; answer is there&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4105 · 2020-05-21T09:12:59:&lt;/b&gt; First or zero&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; “answer is there”; “First or zero.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms the other-door answer is in the first/zero puzzle piece; does not define every use of first/zero." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="6282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-025" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-08-02 · Telegram 4590&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4590 · 2020-08-02T19:56:20:&lt;/b&gt; Really nobody managed to find the extra door, didn&amp;#x27;t expect that after the earlier pace of cracking things.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Asks why nobody found the “extra door.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms another door is literal progression." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="147" width="1860" x="20" y="6471" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-026" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2020-08-12 · Telegram 4688, 4694, 4696&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4688 · 2020-08-12T16:10:55:&lt;/b&gt; Indeed remarkable with the hints stating the path pretty obvious...&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4694 · 2020-08-12T21:23:21:&lt;/b&gt; There&amp;#x27;s 1 club that passed but they are stuck in the next phase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #4696 · 2020-08-12T22:18:55:&lt;/b&gt; Correct&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says the hints make the path “pretty obvious,” one club passed, and confirms it is the next stage of the second route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Strong route/progress confirmation, but no extraction rule." vertex="1">
