        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-032" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2021-04-16 · Telegram 7418&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #7416:&lt;/b&gt; Just do what is told all the time over and over. Go to the first puzzle piece (image) and hash all the text you see. But mind that the author is a bit picky what he considers to be text.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #7418 · 2021-04-16T15:08:24:&lt;/b&gt; Good point&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Replies “Good point” to advice to return to the first image and hash its text, while warning that “text” is picky.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Praise is real, but it does not uniquely confirm every part of the community prescription." vertex="1">
