        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-056" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2024-03-26 · Telegram 23151&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #23148:&lt;/b&gt; @SoWut could you at least tell us which hints are no longer relevant, usually we get one tiny question puzzle related to ask you, last time it was wasted&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #23151 · 2024-03-26T16:40:01:&lt;/b&gt; Technically yes but Nope.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Asked which old hints remain relevant, replies “Technically yes but Nope.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Too ambiguous to reopen or close any specific clue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="12721" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-057" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2024-11-29 · Telegram 32579&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #32579 · 2024-11-29T12:28:47:&lt;/b&gt; At this point, I don&amp;#x27;t know what to hint, without ruining it for those that might find it. If you guys got 1 microstep further, the puzzle will likely be solved the same day.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I could come up with some empty cryptic bs hint, but that would be lame too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;And in the end, good puzzles don&amp;#x27;t need hints, hence this puzzle appears to be a tiny bit shitty sometimes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says one more “microstep” would likely lead to a same-day solve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Prioritizes a local transition over another broad cipher search." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="222" width="1860" x="20" y="12910" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-058" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2025-04-28 · Telegram 39224, 39237&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #39224 · 2025-04-28T19:57:17:&lt;/b&gt; Did anyone found yingyang? I don&amp;#x27;t think so, you guys are so smart, when yingyang is reached, 2 hours max.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #39233:&lt;/b&gt; is yinyang found after decoding an AES ciphertext?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #39237 · 2025-04-28T20:01:36:&lt;/b&gt; It’s the next phase, but I await the day someone finally gets there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says reaching ying-yang leaves at most two hours and explicitly calls it “the next phase.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Strong confirmation that yin-yang is the next reached phase." vertex="1">
