        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-061" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2026-03-04 · Telegram 60312&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent community context #60310 (not a direct reply edge):&lt;/b&gt; Looks at DG&amp;#x27;s comment &amp;quot;its in front of your eyes but you&amp;#x27;re not seeing it&amp;quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #60312 · 2026-03-04T03:29:05:&lt;/b&gt; Bingo&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says Bingo immediately after gnomad repeats only “it’s in front of your eyes but you’re not seeing it.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Confirms the phrase-level pointer, not Looking Forward." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="13824" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-062" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2026-03-04 · Telegram 60314&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adjacent community context #60313 (not a direct reply edge):&lt;/b&gt; Well, @SoWut , let me kindly ask. You&amp;#x27;ve said that no one hit ying-yang yet. If I say that someone applied specific prime inexes to specific last words and extracted like 30 to 31 bytes, that include both &amp;quot;ying yang&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;salvation&amp;quot;, would you change your mind?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #60314 · 2026-03-04T03:30:47:&lt;/b&gt; I only need to look at the address. If any of you reaches the next phase, the price is taken in no-time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says reaching the next phase means the prize is taken “in no-time.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Final transition is short; no algorithm disclosed." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="192" width="1860" x="20" y="14013" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-063" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2026-03-04 · Telegram 60326&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #60323:&lt;/b&gt; i must ask you does the binary contact info from the website jrk.agency have anything to do with the puzzle jrk.xlsx?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #60326 · 2026-03-04T03:36:04:&lt;/b&gt; Nope. You&amp;#x27;re not the first to ask.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Replies “Nope” to whether binary contact information on jrk.agency is related.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Closes that external-site lead." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="177" width="1860" x="20" y="14217" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-064" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2026-05-28 · Telegram 63957&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Community parent #63942:&lt;/b&gt; @SoWut  The sites are down. Can you tell us whether this will affect us if we manage to resolve Salp or Cosmic? We&amp;#x27;re worried about relying on another site and it no longer existing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #63957 · 2026-05-28T14:41:02:&lt;/b&gt; Ah, ofcourse. The puzzle is still valid!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; When the sites go offline, confirms “The puzzle is still valid!”&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Solving does not depend on the removed live sites." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="192" width="1860" x="20" y="14406" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-section-07" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;" value="July 2026 Creator Return — 8 panels" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1860" x="20" y="14626" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creator-evidence-card-065" parent="creator-evidence-lane" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;2026-07-13 · Telegram 66568&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Source:&lt;/i&gt; GSMG Puzzle Solvers&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Creator #66568 · 2026-07-13T03:47:16:&lt;/b&gt; Most of you know the puzzle WAAAY better than me at this point. I have a hidden laptop which I haven&amp;#x27;t touched in years. On that thing... is the actual answer....&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Indexed evidence:&lt;/b&gt; Says the actual answer is on a hidden laptop untouched for years.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meaning / limit:&lt;/b&gt; Establishes retained ground truth, not a cryptographic clue by itself." vertex="1">
